 The pinned CR file and local Oracle fixtures are the evidence sources. Live Scryfall access belongs to the online/periodic lane and is not an ordinary acceptance prerequisite.
+
+<!-- clause: ENG-COMP-005 -->
+The Oracle compiler is one automation mechanism among manual operations, deterministic recognizers, finite evaluators, and card-specific implementations. Its `auto`, `guided`, and `manual` decision tiers describe how a compiled clause is handled; they do not define OneDeck's overall maturity or require broader Oracle compilation as a product goal. A General Rules Engine is a separate architecture choice.
+
+<!-- clause: ENG-COMP-006 -->
+The compiler may support a deterministic leaf without generating structured UI for every unsupported sibling. Unknown meaning remains human-owned, and repeated human friction is evaluated as an automation investment signal rather than answered by adding mandatory confirmation prompts by default.

